        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- Plants: Sparaxis, Campanula, Dierama pendulum, Hawaiian lobelioids\n- Plant families: Iridaceae, Campanulaceae\n- Places: Cape Province, South Africa, Hawaiian Islands\n\nFacts:\n- Sparaxis is a genus in the family Iridaceae with about 13 species endemic to Cape Province, South Africa.\n- Campanula is one of several genera in the family Campanulaceae that share the common name bellflower.\n- Before its current classification, Dierama pendulum had been placed in the genera Ixia, Sparaxis, and Watsonia.\n- The Hawaiian lobelioids are a group of flowering plants in the family Campanulaceae that are endemic to the Hawaiian Islands.",
